      'Turn-flow example: Players bid once in turn with higher contracts over lower. Some contracts create a temporary partner via called ace or king; others are solo contracts. Winning bid determines trump suit and contract objective. Play 8 tricks with follow-suit required. If void in led suit, player may trump or discard. Highest trump wins trick; otherwise highest of led suit. Trick winner leads next.',
      'Scoring example: Contract winner side wins or loses hand value based on meeting trick target; many tables include optional macker and first-last bonuses. Complete your declared contract target; otherwise defenders set and collect..',
